Chapter: FactDiskHostileHead
  cites Foreword chapter FactDisk
  cites Foreword chapter ImportGate
  cites Foreword chapter FactStore
  cites Foreword chapter Hamt
  cites Foreword chapter Maybe

 The factdisk-read vector with two fields moved, and nothing else:

   superblock log head   5 -> 8,000,000   far past the 2048-sector medium
   sector 3 content len  49 -> 4,000,000,000

 Those two are one defect rather than two, and the head is the half that
 enables it. fd-fold-entry bounds an entry's sector span on
 `sector + nsec > end-sec`, and end-sec IS the head, so with an honest head of
 5 the 4e9 entry is already refused by the code as it stood. Only a head that
 is itself a lie admits it: 4,000,000,000 bytes spans 7,812,501 sectors and
 ends at 7,812,504, which clears a head of 8,000,000, and fd-entry-content
 then asks alloc-bytes for 4,000,000,512 bytes on a 3 GB guest.

 So the store is refused whole rather than read up to where it stops making
 sense. The positive control moves accordingly: it is no longer "the good
 entry still arrives" but "the bundle we were handed is given back intact".
 A refusal that also dropped the caller's own facts would pass a count check
 and lose the compiler its offered works.

 codex/test/apps/factdisk-read is the other half of the control and is
 deliberately left untouched: same reader, honest superblock, all three
 entries still walked.

 We say:

Section: Reading a fact back

  show-fact : Maybe Fact -> Text
  show-fact (m) =
    when m
     is None -> "absent"
     is Just (f) -> f.content & "/" & f.author & "/" & show (f.timestamp)

Section: A bundle the caller already holds

  prior : Fact
  prior = Fact {
    hash = "zzz999",
    kind = DefinitionFact,
    content = "from the blob",
    author = "base",
    timestamp = 1
  }

Section: Body

  opening : [Console, Device.Block] Nothing = act
    fresh <- store-read-bundle bundle-empty
    print-line-uni ("count=" & show (fact-count (fresh.facts)))
    print-line-uni ("lying-entry=" & show-fact (fact-load (fresh.facts) "abc123"))
    print-line-uni ("honest-entry=" & show-fact (fact-load (fresh.facts) "def456"))
    supplemented <- store-read-bundle (bundle-offer bundle-empty prior)
    print-line-uni ("supplemented-count=" & show (fact-count (supplemented.facts)))
    print-line-uni ("caller-fact-survives=" & show-fact (fact-load (supplemented.facts) "zzz999"))
  end
